@startmindmap
* Spring Security Advanced Learning
** Authorization and Access Control
*** Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)
**** Define roles and permissions
**** Use @PreAuthorize and @Secured annotations
**** Source: https://spring.io/guides/topicals/spring-security-authorization/
*** URL-based Security
**** Configure HttpSecurity for URL patterns
**** Use antMatchers and mvcMatchers
**** Source: https://docs.spring.io/spring-security/reference/servlet/authorization/
** JWT and Token-Based Authentication
*** JWT Basics
**** Structure: Header, Payload, Signature
**** Use cases: stateless authentication
**** Source: https://jwt.io/introduction/
*** Implementing JWT in Spring
**** Use filters to validate tokens
**** Store user details in SecurityContext
**** Source: https://www.baeldung.com/spring-security-oauth-jwt
** OAuth2 and OpenID Connect
*** OAuth2 Basics
**** Roles: Resource Owner, Client, Authorization Server, Resource Server
**** Grant types: Authorization Code, Implicit, Client Credentials
**** Source: https://oauth.net/2/
*** OpenID Connect
**** Adds identity layer on OAuth2
**** Provides user info and authentication
**** Source: https://openid.net/connect/
** Method Security with Annotations
*** @PreAuthorize
**** Expression-based access control
**** Example: @PreAuthorize("hasRole('ADMIN')")
*** @Secured
**** Role-based method security
**** Example: @Secured("ROLE_USER")
*** @PostAuthorize
**** Checks after method execution
**** Example: @PostAuthorize("returnObject.owner == authentication.name")
** Security Testing
*** Unit Testing
**** Mock authentication objects
**** Use @WithMockUser
**** Source: https://docs.spring.io/spring-security/site/docs/current/reference/html5/#test
*** Integration Testing
**** Test security filters and endpoints
**** Use MockMvc with security
** Custom Authentication Providers
*** Creating Custom Provider
**** Implement AuthenticationProvider interface
**** Handle custom token or credential types
*** Use Cases
**** Multi-factor authentication
**** External system integration
** Session Management and CSRF Protection
*** Session Fixation
**** Prevent session fixation attacks
**** Use session management strategies
*** CSRF Protection
**** Enable CSRF tokens
**** Use with state-changing requests
** Security Best Practices and Hardening
*** Password Policies
**** Enforce strong passwords
**** Use BCrypt with strength factor
*** Secure Headers
**** Configure HTTP headers (CSP, HSTS)
**** Prevent clickjacking and XSS
*** Logging and Monitoring
**** Audit security events
**** Monitor suspicious activities
@endmindmap